  "grammarNotes": [
    {
      "id": "woher-present-tense",
      "title": "Present tense: regular verbs",
      "body": "Take the infinitive, remove **-en** to get the stem (*lern-en → lern-*), then add the ending for the person.\n\n- **wir**, **sie** (they) and **Sie** (formal you) always look like the infinitive\n- **er**, **sie** (she) and **ihr** all end in **-t**\n\nGerman has only one present tense: *ich lerne* means both *I learn* and *I am learning*.",
      "table": [
        ["Person", "Ending", "lernen", "wohnen", "kommen"],
        ["ich", "-e", "lerne", "wohne", "komme"],
        ["du", "-st", "lernst", "wohnst", "kommst"],
        ["er / sie / es", "-t", "lernt", "wohnt", "kommt"],
        ["wir", "-en", "lernen", "wohnen", "kommen"],
        ["ihr", "-t", "lernt", "wohnt", "kommt"],
        ["sie / Sie", "-en", "lernen", "wohnen", "kommen"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "woher-sprechen",
      "title": "sprechen: e changes to i",
      "body": "Some verbs change their vowel in the **du** and **er/sie/es** forms only. *sprechen* is one of them: the *e* becomes *i*. The endings stay regular.",
      "table": [
        ["Person", "sprechen"],
        ["ich", "spreche"],
        ["du", "sprichst"],
        ["er / sie / es", "spricht"],
        ["wir", "sprechen"],
        ["ihr", "sprecht"],
        ["sie / Sie", "sprechen"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "woher-sie",
      "title": "sie, sie or Sie?",
      "body": "The same word has three meanings. The verb ending and the capital letter tell them apart:\n\n- **sie** + *-t* = she: *sie wohnt*\n- **sie** + *-en* = they: *sie wohnen*\n- **Sie** + *-en*, always capitalised = you (formal): *Sie wohnen*\n\nAt the start of a sentence, *she/they* are capitalised too, so context decides."
    },
    {
      "id": "woher-w-questions",
      "title": "W-questions",
      "body": "Question words start with **w**, and the verb comes **second**, right after the question word.\n\nCareful: **wer** means *who* and **wo** means *where*. They look like the English words swapped around!",
      "table": [
        ["German", "English", "Example"],
        ["wer", "who", "Wer ist das?"],
        ["was", "what", "Was machst du?"],
        ["wo", "where", "Wo wohnst du?"],
        ["woher", "where from", "Woher kommst du?"],
        ["wie", "how", "Wie heißt du?"]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "woher-countries",
      "title": "Countries",
      "body": "Most countries have no article: *aus Deutschland, aus Österreich, aus England*.\n\nA few are feminine and need **der** after *aus*: **die Schweiz → aus der Schweiz**, **die Türkei → aus der Türkei**. A couple are plural: **die USA → aus den USA**."
    }
  ],
